# When two branches each add their own entry to CHANGELOG.md's
# [Unreleased] section, git's default merge produces a conflict even
# though the right resolution is "keep both." `merge=union` tells git
# to take both sides of conflicting hunks, in order, with no markers.
# This is the right behavior for append-only logs like a CHANGELOG.
#
# It is NOT the right behavior for source code; do not extend this rule
# casually. If you find yourself wanting it for another file, think
# hard about whether you really mean "additive log" or whether you
# should be reordering or de-duping entries by hand.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union

# infra/README.md is the same shape as CHANGELOG.md: a flat list where
# every infra PR appends one line about the module it added. Manually
# resolving these "both branches added an entry" conflicts is mechanical
# noise (literally hand-resolved 4 times in a single drain pass on
# 2026-05-08). Same fix as CHANGELOG: union the two sides at conflict
# time, no markers.
#
# Trade-off: union may end up with the new entries in a non-alphabetical
# order. Acceptable for an append-only "modules" list. If we ever need
# this file to be strictly ordered (alphabetical, dependency-ordered,
# etc.), drop merge=union and resolve by hand. Don't extend this rule
# to other README files casually.
infra/README.md merge=union
